course: dictionary
lesson: 3443
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Fabric is one of them. A fabric is cloth, but the fabric of a building means its walls, floors and roof.
explain: Read «Light bulbs get hot, so lamps and nightlights are kept away from curtains and other fabric.» Curtains are made of cloth, so fabric here means cloth. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Cloth fits, so that is the meaning.
explain: In «the fabric of society», fabric does not mean cloth at all. It means the basic structure that holds society together. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense: «the basic structure of society» works, so you have it right.
fact: Fabric means cloth, material made by weaving or knitting threads.
fact: The fabric of a building means its walls, floors and roof.
fact: The fabric of society or life means the basic structure that holds it together.
fact: «Cotton fabric», «waterproof fabric» and «a piece of fabric» all mean cloth.
fact: «Fabric softener» is a liquid you add to the wash to make clothes feel soft.
exercise: «Cotton fluff is spun into thread, knitted into fabric, and sewn into a T-shirt.» What is the fabric in this sentence? | The walls and roof of a building | *Cloth made by knitting threads | The main structure that holds a country together | A kind of cotton plant
exercise: «The fabric of the old school was cracked, with leaking roofs and damp walls.» What does fabric mean here? | The people who live in a town | Warm, soft wool | Cloth used for curtains | *The walls, floors and roof of a building
exercise: «Fabric scissors are kept only for cloth, because cutting paper or card makes the blades blunt.» What does fabric mean in «fabric scissors»? | Paper or card | *Cloth or material | The walls of a building | The structure of society
test: In «the fabric of society», fabric means: | *The basic structure that holds it together | A soft blanket | A waterproof coat | Cloth made from threads
test: Which of these is a fabric a designer could choose for a project? | Sunshine | *Felt | Hammer | Pencil
exam: Which sentence uses fabric to mean cloth? | *«The waterproof fabric kept the rain off our tents.» | «The fabric of the house was cracked and damp.» | «The fabric of the school needs urgent repairs.» | «The fabric of society is strong and fair.»
